<p>
  The CRM module follows a sale from first contact to signed deal. It's built around three ideas:
  <strong>leads</strong>
  (people who might buy), <strong>deals</strong>
  (an opportunity with a value) and <strong>tasks</strong>
  (the next thing to do).
</p>

<h2>Leads</h2>
<p>
  Add everyone who shows interest to <.link navigate="/leads">Leads</.link>: website sign-ups, event
  contacts, referrals. Update the status as you qualify them.
</p>
<p>
  When a lead is real, open it and click <strong>Convert</strong>. Zippiker creates the contact,
  their company and (optionally) a deal in one go, and keeps the lead for your records.
</p>

<h2>The deal board</h2>
<p>
  <.link navigate="/deals">Deals</.link>
  shows your pipeline as columns. Drag a card to move it to the next
  stage. Each stage has a win probability, which powers the <em>weighted forecast</em>
  on the dashboard.
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    Moving a deal to <strong>Won</strong>
    or <strong>Lost</strong>
    closes it (lost deals ask for a reason).
  </li>
  <li>Accepting a quote linked to a deal marks the deal as won automatically.</li>
  <li>
    Admins can rename, reorder and add stages in <.link navigate="/settings/pipeline">Settings → Pipeline</.link>.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Activities and tasks</h2>
<p>
  On any contact, company or deal, log calls, emails, meetings and notes so the whole team knows
  what happened. Add tasks with a due date; they appear on your dashboard agenda and in <.link navigate="/tasks">Tasks</.link>, where overdue ones are highlighted.
</p>
<.callout>
  Tip: after every customer conversation, log it and create the next task before you close the page.
  Your pipeline stays honest and nothing falls through the cracks.
</.callout>
